To find the point of intersection, we can solve the system of equations:
\begin{align*}
y &= 4x - 19 \\
2x + y &= 95
\end{align*}
Substituting the first equation into the second equation, we get:
\begin{align*}
2x + 4x - 19 &= 95 \\
6x &= 114 \\
x &= \frac{114}{6} \\
x &= 19
\end{align*}
So the value of $x$ at the point of intersection is $\boxed{19}$.The answer is: 19

