We can use long division to divide $2x^4+11x^3-42x^2-60x+47$ by $x^2+7x-5$.
The division looks like this:

\[
\begin{array}{c|cc cc cc}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{2x^2} & +25x & +119 \\
\cline{2-7}
x^2+7x-5 & 2x^4 & +11x^3 & -42x^2 & -60x & +47 \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{-2x^4} & -14x^3 & +10x^2 \\ \cline{2-4}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & -3x^3 & -32x^2 & -60x \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & +3x^3 & +21x^2 & -15x \\ \cline{3-5}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & -11x^2 & -75x & +47 \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & +11x^2 & +77x & -55 \\ \cline{4-6}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & & 2x & -8 \\
\end{array}
\]

The remainder is $2x-8$.

