We can rewrite the numerator and denominator as geometric series:
\begin{align*}
2+4-8+16+32-64 &= 2(1-2+4-8+16-32) \\
&= 2\left(\frac{1-(-2)^6}{1-(-2)}\right) \\
&= 2\left(\frac{1-64}{1+2}\right) \\
&= 2\left(\frac{-63}{3}\right) \\
&= -42.
\end{align*}
\begin{align*}
4+8-16+32+64-128 &= 4(1+2-4+8-16+32) \\
&= 4\left(\frac{1-(-2)^6}{1-(-2)}\right) \\
&= 4\left(\frac{1-64}{1+2}\right) \\
&= 4\left(\frac{-63}{3}\right) \\
&= -84.
\end{align*}
Therefore, $\frac{2+4-8+16+32-64}{4+8-16+32+64-128} = \frac{-42}{-84} = \boxed{\frac{1}{2}}$.The answer is: \frac{1}{2}

